/The-periodic-spin-one-Haldane-gap-September-24-2026/build/introduction.tex","line":37,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"e6c0f0c1df097342c668fcc72e2d32da23c329133a4942cafacf0d32135fad8c","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/The-periodic-spin-one-Haldane-gap-September-24-2026/build/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:f0ac3a7089a8b36212b38e5fecf36c09eeda59c97b358b45cb57a50fa34c8adb","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/The-periodic-spin-one-Haldane-gap-September-24-2026/build/introduction.tex#L37"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nFor the Hamiltonians \\eqref{eq:main-H}, the ground state is unique for\nevery even $L\\ge60$, and\n\\begin{align}\n \\gamma_L&>\\frac4{105}\\log\\frac{80}{79}\n     &&\\text{for every even }L\\ge60,\\label{eq:gap60}\\\\\n \\gamma_L&>\\frac{\\log20}{784}\n     &&\\text{for every even }L\\ge2304.\\label{eq:gap2304}\n\\end{align}\nConsequently\n\\[\n \\Delta_1\\ge\\frac{\\log20}{784}>0.\n\\]\nThe spectral conclusions also hold for any simultaneously similar\nspin-one realization satisfying the same commutator and Casimir\nnormalizations."}
